  "headroom_paint": {
    "prompt": 45,
    "date": "2026-09-04",
    "what": "The ground rect is drawn from y=-90 instead of y=0 and the root <svg> is overflow:visible, so the artwork paints the iOS safe-area band above the stage instead of leaving it to .banner's CSS gradient. That boundary was the seam Joe reported: 8.7/255 under the wordmark, 10.7 under the TV, 3.1 on neutral ground. Measured after: 2.0 worst.",
    "gradients": "bnBg, bnGlow0 and bnGlow1 were objectBoundingBox (the default), so growing a shape would have stretched its gradient with it. All three are gradientUnits=userSpaceOnUse now, pinned to stage coordinates; the two radial ones carry the box aspect as a gradientTransform. Arithmetic: artifacts/qa/2026-09-05-banner-seam/gradient-convert.py.",
    "unchanged": "Every mark, image, text and filter coordinate below is exactly as generated, and the glow ellipses are NOT extended - see BannerMobileV2.jsx for why their outer stops keep their tails. The 0-155 stage region measured 8 of 597060 pixels different by 1/255 at 428 CSS px / DPR 3, which is Chromium's gradient rasteriser, not a geometry change.",
    "rect": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -90,
      "w": 428,
      "h": 245,
      "note": "y = -overhang, h = overhang + stage.h. The generator derives h from stage.h so the ground cannot be left behind when the stage changes height."
    }
  },
  "_gold": "Metallic gold family, prompt 52 stage 4. Mapped from docs/ux-reference/visual-refinement-handoff-2026-09-06.md §4: #FBE59A->#E0D1A5 highlight, #F2CD62->#C6AF7A primary, #E4B646->#B39A69 mid, #D2A038->#8C7650 deep, and the wordmark's blurred glow copy #F3CC5A->#C6AF7A. The rgb(255,170,60) ambient ellipses and the rgb(255,150,40) TV halo are NOT the wordmark - they are §7's charcoal-spotlight background, which §7 says to retain. GEOMETRY IS UNTOUCHED: artboard, type size, letter-spacing and every coordinate are byte-identical. Colour only."
